# Ruleset: Telemetry
#
# Expects a reject policy.
#
# Usage telemetry, product analytics and crash reports that the imported reject layer lets through, so they would otherwise ride a proxy exit. Developer CLIs are the heaviest senders: they report on every command. Hang this on a policy that can be switched off rather than a hard REJECT.
#
# Scope: the ingestion host, never the vendor's dashboard or API, which keep their own file or FINAL. Feature flag services stay out, because a client that cannot fetch its flags changes behavior. Our own services stay in Developer/Owned.list. A host whose company list sits in the overlay, ahead of the reject block (GitHub, AI, Tailscale coordination), cannot be caught here.

# Cloudflare: wrangler's usage events.
DOMAIN,sparrow.cloudflare.com

# Vercel: the CLI and Turborepo.
DOMAIN,telemetry.vercel.com

# Sentry ingestion, per region. sentry.io itself stays in Developer/Sentry.list.
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,ingest.sentry.io
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,ingest.us.sentry.io
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,ingest.de.sentry.io

# Datadog log and browser intake. The us5 browser intake is its own registrable domain.
DOMAIN,http-intake.logs.datadoghq.com
DOMAIN,http-intake.logs.us5.datadoghq.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,browser-intake-datadoghq.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,browser-intake-us5-datadoghq.com

# PostHog ingestion. posthog.com itself is the product site.
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,i.posthog.com
DOMAIN,app.posthog.com

# Segment
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,segment.io
DOMAIN,cdn-settings.segment.com

# 1Password usage and crash reports. The vaults stay in Developer/1Password.list.
DOMAIN,telemetry.1passwordservices.com
DOMAIN,b5x-sentry.1passwordservices.com

# Microsoft App Center
DOMAIN,in.appcenter.ms

# Firebase Crashlytics
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,crashlytics.com
DOMAIN,crashlyticsreports-pa.googleapis.com

# Tailscale's log service. Clients keep working without it.
DOMAIN,log.tailscale.com

# X web analytics
DOMAIN,analytics.twitter.com
